// Crawly Frontier API: runs (scheduler API).
//
// Run termination: a run COMPLETES when it is sealed AND it has no pending, delayed or
// in-flight tasks. It ends early in one of three ways, and the remaining tasks are dropped
// in each of them (counted as expired for the first, as cancelled for the other two):
//   - EXPIRED: its deadline is reached.
//   - CANCELLED: an operator or scheduler called CancelRun.
//   - ABORTED: one of the rules of RunLimits (abort_on_codes, max_failed,
//     max_consecutive_failures) tripped. The Frontier ends the run in the same
//     transaction that applies the outcome; Run.abort_reason says which rule and which
//     task. A run that is already over is not aborted, so a run has one reason at most.
// Leases of the dropped tasks are revoked in all three cases.

